    "distance_$length_unit": "行驶里程",
    "efficiency_$length_unit": "基准电耗",
    "end_date": "结束时间",
    "maxrange_$length_unit": "新车满电续航（估算）",
    "mileage_$length_unit": "累计里程",
    "odometer": "里程表读数",
    "odometer_$length_unit": "里程表读数",
    "range_$length_unit": "剩余续航",
    "range_lost_$length_unit": "续航减少量",
    "speed_$length_unit": "平均车速",
    "start_date": "开始时间",
    "time": "时间",
    "charging (AC)": "交流充电",
    "charging (DC)": "直流充电",
    "Total Energy added (AC)": "累计交流充入电量",
    "Total Energy added (DC)": "累计直流充入电量"
  },
  "descriptions": {
    "\"# of Charging cycles\" is estimated by dividing the whole energy added to the battery by the battery capacity when new.\n\n\"Charging Efficiency\" is estimated on the difference between energy used from the charger and energy added to the battery.": "“等效完整充电循环次数”＝累计充入电池的电量 ÷ 新车可用电池容量。例如，两次各充入相当于电池容量 50% 的电量，约合一个完整循环；不是插枪次数。\n\n“充电效率”根据充电端耗电量与充入电池的电量估算，两者之差包含充电转换及相关辅助用电。",
    "\"Logged\" is the distance traveled that is saved on TeslaMate database.\n\n\"Mileage\" is the distance the car has traveled since using TeslaMate.\n\nSo, if there is a difference between both values, it is the distance that for some reason a drive hasn't been fully recorded, for example due to a bug or an unexpected restart and that TeslaMate has not been able to record, either due to lack of connection, areas without signal, or that it has been out of service.": "“已记录里程”是数据库中完整记录下来的行程里程之和；“累计里程”是开始使用 TeslaMate 后，车辆里程表增加的里程。\n\n两者之差表示未被完整记录的行驶里程，可能由网络中断、无信号、服务停止或异常重启造成，不代表车辆里程表错误。",
    "(Range lost * Efficiency) / Distance driven": "根据续航变化和基准电耗估算用车总耗电量，再除以行驶里程，包含停车、待机等非行驶耗电。不包含充电桩到电池之间的充电损耗，不能直接当作购电电耗。",
    "(Range lost while driving * Efficiency) / Distance driven": "根据行驶期间减少的续航里程乘以车辆基准电耗，估算行驶耗电量，再除以实际行驶里程。包含能量回收的净影响；不是直接读取电表得出的电耗。",
    "**Usable (now)** is the estimated current battery capacity. It is average of the estimated capacity reported by the last 10 charging sessions to have a better estimation.\n\nIf you see just '1.0 kWh' here, it means that you need at least a long charge session.\n\n**Usable (new)** is the estimated Battery Capacity since you begun to use TeslaMate. That's why, the more data you have logged from your brand new car the better. For those who have not used TeslaMate since they got their new car, or for those who have bought it second hand,  it's possible to set the max range to 100% and the battery capacity of the car battery when it was new in order to get a better and accurate estimation.": "**当前可用容量（估算）**：最近 10 次有效充电记录推算出的电池可用容量的平均值，用于减小单次记录的波动。如果只显示 1.0 kWh，通常说明缺少足够长、数据充分的充电记录。\n\n**新车可用容量（估算）**：根据开始使用 TeslaMate 后的记录推算。越早开始记录新车数据，参考价值越高。如果是二手车或较晚才开始记录，可在上方填写已知的新车可用电池容量和新车满电续航，避免把记录起点误当作新车状态。这里是可用容量，不是电池铭牌上的总容量。",
    "<b>Shared Buffers:</b> This metric shows the amount of memory PostgreSQL uses to store frequently accessed data, like tables and indexes, to make queries faster by avoiding slow disk reads.\n\n<b>Recommended value:</b> Use about 25% of your system's total RAM (e.g., 1GB for a system with 4GB RAM). Start with a modest value and adjust based on your app's needs. Setting it too high can waste memory.\n\n<b>To change in a Postgres Docker Compose file:</b> In your docker-compose.yml, add or update the command field under the Postgres service to include the shared_buffers setting. For example:\n\n<pre>\nservices:\n  database:\n    image: postgres:18-trixie\n    command: postgres -c shared_buffers=1GB\n    ...\n</pre>\n\nAfter updating the file, run <code>docker compose down</code> and <code>docker compose up -d</code> to restart the container and apply the change.\n\nFor more details: <a href='https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-resource.html#GUC-SHARED-BUFFERS' target='_blank'>PostgreSQL: Documentation: 18: 19.4. Resource Consumption</a>": "<b>数据库共享缓存（shared_buffers）</b>用于保存经常访问的数据表和索引，减少磁盘读取。\n\n官方一般建议从机器总内存的约 25% 起步，但同一台机器可能还运行其他服务，不能机械套用。此处只显示状态，不会修改配置。需要调整时，应先评估全部应用的内存需求并按 <a href=\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-resource.html#GUC-SHARED-BUFFERS\" target=\"_blank\">PostgreSQL 官方说明</a>操作；单纯调整缓存不需要删除数据卷。",
    "A high level overview of your car": "车辆当前状态、充电、温度、电量及续航概况。",
    "Blue: route driven in the selected time range. Orange: each city where a drive started/ended or the car charged. Hover a marker for dates; click the city name to see every day spent there.": "蓝线：所选时段内的行驶轨迹。橙色标记：行程开始、结束或发生充电的城市。悬停可查看日期；点击城市名称可查看在该城市的每日记录。",
    "Browse your charges by Geofence, Location, Type, Cost and Duration in order to have an accurate Total of kWh added and their respective costs": "按常用地点、地址、充电类型、费用和时长筛选充电记录，汇总相应的充入电量和费用。“每度电”中的一度电等于 1 kWh；费用币种沿用原有设置，不进行汇率换算。",
    "Check the [contribution docs](https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/development#enable-pg_stat_statements-to-collect-query-statistics) on how to enable tracking planning and execution statistics of all SQL statements executed by a server.\n": "如需跟踪 SQL 查询的规划与执行用时，请参阅[官方配置说明](https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/development#enable-pg_stat_statements-to-collect-query-statistics)。本页不自动启用扩展或更改数据库。",
    "Click a city to list every day you were there.": "点击城市可查看到访该城市的日期。",
    "Comma separated list of locations to exclude. Ex: home, work": "输入需要排除的地点名称，用英文逗号分隔，例如：家,公司。应与已记录的地点名称一致。",
    "Data used to calculate Moving Average / Percentiles is unevenly sampled in TeslaMate. To avoid biases towards more frequently sampled values, the data is bucketed. For buckets without sampled values, the last observed value is carried forward. Bucketing is not time-weighted but is a simple average. Increasing the bucket width results in a loss of accuracy.": "车辆数据的采样间隔并不均匀。为避免采样密集时段占据过大权重，先按固定时间段分组；没有采样值的分组延用上一次观测值。每组使用普通平均值，不按采样间隔加权。分组时间越长，细节和精度损失越多。百分位数用于观察波动范围，不是统计置信区间。",
    "Days in the selected city for the car selected in the Cities table or on the map. Click a date to open that day in the Drives dashboard.": "显示在城市表格或地图中选定的车辆与城市的每日记录。点击日期，可在“行程记录”中查看当天的行程。",
    "Distance of all logged drives": "所选时段内已记录行程的里程之和，可能小于车辆里程表的实际增加量。",
    "For each day the thin line runs from the lowest to the highest temperature recorded, while the thicker bar shows the 15th–85th percentile range (the temperatures between which 70% of the day’s readings fell). Days with no readings are left blank.\n\nNote: On days with only partial coverage (for example just a few hours of data), the shown range only reflects the periods that were actually measured and may not represent the full day. The red line shows the data coverage for each day.": "细线表示当天记录到的最低至最高温度，色块下边界是 15% 分位温度，上边界是 85% 分位温度：将当天温度读数从低到高排列，分别取 15% 和 85% 位置的温度。两者之间包含中间约 70% 的读数（85% − 15%），并不是温度或电量的百分比。没有读数的日期留空。\n\n若某天只有部分时段有记录，图中范围只代表这些实际采样时段，不等于全天气温。红线表示每天的数据覆盖率；此图也不等同于气象站测得的环境温度。",
    "From here you can check if you have \nincomplete data of **Charges** (charges without ending date)\nIf so, you may follow the official \nguide by <a href='https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/maintenance/manually_fixing_data' target='_blank'>Manually fixing data</a>": "这里显示尚无结束时间的充电记录，其中可能包含正在进行的正常充电。请先查看详情，不要直接当作损坏数据删除。确认记录异常后，可参阅<a href=\"https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/maintenance/manually_fixing_data\" target=\"_blank\">官方数据修复说明</a>。",
    "From here you can check if you have \nincomplete data of **Drives** (drives without ending date)\nIf so, you may follow the official \nguide by <a href='https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/maintenance/manually_fixing_data' target='_blank'>Manually fixing data</a>": "这里显示尚无结束时间的行程记录，其中可能包含正在进行的正常行驶。请先查看详情，不要直接当作损坏数据删除。确认记录异常后，可参阅<a href=\"https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/maintenance/manually_fixing_data\" target=\"_blank\">官方数据修复说明</a>。",
    "In cold weather, the estimated range loss cannot be estimated correctly and is therefore hidden.": "低温时，部分电量可能暂时不可用，续航减少量不能可靠换算成停车耗电，因此隐藏此项估算。",
    "Only End Battery Level of last Charging Process considered for consecutive Charging Processes": "连续多段充电按一组统计时，只采用最后一段结束时的电量，避免重复计数。",
    "Only Start Battery Level of first Charging Process considered for consecutive Charging Processes": "连续多段充电按一组统计时，只采用第一段开始时的电量，避免重复计数。",
    "Only distinguishes between online, offline and asleep.": "此项只区分在线、离线和休眠，不单独区分行驶、充电等活动。",
    "Open **Drives** or **Charges** can be active sessions and are not necessarily incomplete. Select a count to review the matching records.\nIf a record is incomplete, follow the official guide: \n<a href='https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/maintenance/manually_fixing_data' target='_blank'>Manually fixing data</a>": "尚未结束的行程或充电可能仍在进行，并不一定是异常数据。点击数量可查看对应记录。\n\n确认记录异常后，再参阅<a href=\"https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/maintenance/manually_fixing_data\" target=\"_blank\">官方数据修复说明</a>。",
    "Select how Efficiency ratings should be calculated.\n\n\"by distance\" is doing a simple comparison based on distance driven and range lost while driving.\n\n\"slope-adjusted\" takes ascent / descent of the drive into account and adjusts the energy consumed accordingly. regen breaking efficiency is set to 85% and the vehicle is assumed to have a weight of 2100 kg.": "选择续航达成率的估算方式。\n\n“按里程计算”：比较实际行驶里程与行驶期间减少的续航里程。\n\n“考虑上下坡”：根据爬升和下降对耗电估算作修正，算法假定整车质量为 2100 kg、能量回收效率为 85%。这两个值是算法假设，并非对这辆车的实测结果。",
    "Set the capacity of your car battery when it was new, in case you started using TeslaMate after a while of having it. If not, leave it at 0, it will be calculated with the data that is logged in TeslaMate": "如果开始记录时车辆已使用一段时间，可填写已知的新车可用电池容量（kWh）。应填写可用容量，不要把电池总容量当作可用容量。没有可靠数据时保持为 0，由已记录的数据估算。",
    "Set the max range to 100% of your car when it was new, in case you started using TeslaMate after a while of having it. If not, leave it at 0, the degradation will be calculated with the data that is logged in TeslaMate": "如果开始记录时车辆已使用一段时间，可填写新车 100% 电量时、与当前续航口径一致的续航里程。不要混用标准续航、理想续航或广告标称 CLTC 续航。没有可靠数据时保持为 0，由已记录的数据估算。",
    "Shared visit data for this car and the selected time range. The summary, Countries and Cities panels reuse this query.": "本车在所选时间段内的到访数据。概况、国家和城市面板共用此查询。",
    "Shows how much energy has been recovered through regenerative braking.\n\n\"Energy recovered\" is already included in \"Energy consumed (net)\" and is determined by looking for periods with negative power within your drive. \n\nRequires Streaming API to be enabled and available for this drive.": "根据行驶期间功率为负的记录，估算制动能量回收带回电池的电量。\n\n这部分回收电量已经计入“行驶耗电量”的扣减，不能再扣一次。只有该次行程启用了数据流 API 且有可用记录时，才有此项数据。",
    "The average is calculated from 15-minute buckets. Coverage shows the proportion of the selected period with logged temperature data; the average only describes periods when the car was logging.": "平均温度先按 15 分钟分组计算。数据覆盖率表示所选时段中，有温度记录的时间所占比例；平均值只代表车辆实际有记录的时段，并不一定代表全天。",
    "These statistics can help you evaluate the efficiency of your indexes.\n\nIf your database experiences a lot of updates or deletions, like importing data from other sources or deleting a loaner car or some other similar situation, you might encounter index bloat, which can degrade performance. In such cases, reindexing could be beneficial.\n\nCheck <a href='https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/maintenance/manually_fixing_data#reindex-database' target='_blank'>Reindex Database</a>": "这些统计用于观察索引的使用情况。大量导入、更新或删除数据后，索引可能占用额外空间并影响查询速度；是否需要重建应结合实际情况判断，不要仅凭某个数值操作。参阅<a href=\"https://docs.teslamate.org/docs/maintenance/manually_fixing_data#reindex-database\" target=\"_blank\">官方索引维护说明</a>。",
    "This dashboard is meant to have a look of the Battery health based on the data logged in TeslaMate. So, the more data you have logged from your brand new car the better.\n\n**Degradation** is just an estimated value to have a reference, measured on **usable battery level** of every charging session with enough kWh added (in order to avoid dirty data from the sample), calculated according to the rated efficiency of the car.": "本页根据 TeslaMate 记录估算电池健康状况，记录越早、有效数据越多，结果通常越有参考价值。\n\n“估算容量衰减”根据有效充电记录中的可用电量及车辆基准电耗推算，过滤充入电量过小的记录以减少误差。这不是厂家检测结果，也不能单独作为电池故障或保修判定依据。",
    "This is the Derived Rated Efficiency that TeslaMate calculates based on battery charges. \nThis information can be seen in more detail on the \"Efficiency\" dashboard.": "这是 TeslaMate 根据充电记录及标准续航变化推算的基准电耗，用于将续航变化换算成电量。它不是实际路况下的百公里电耗。详细分布可查看“能耗分析”仪表盘。",
    "Type a text contained in Location": "输入地点名称或地址中包含的文字。",
    "Type a text contained in Start or Destination Location": "输入出发地点或目的地名称、地址中包含的文字。",
    "When enabled \"Ø Consumption (gross)\" will be calculated via Positions instead of Charging Processes and Drives.\n\nWhile being more accurate (especially for shorter periods) this will be slow on slow hardware!": "开启后，综合电耗使用位置采样记录计算，而不是只使用充电过程和行程的起止数据。短时间段通常更精细，但对数据量大或性能较弱的设备，查询可能明显变慢。计算结果仍是估算值。",
    "based on any data ever recorded.": "根据所有历史记录计算，不只限于当前选择的时间段。"
  },
  "source_ref": "v4.4.0",
